This repository contains multiple components under different licenses.
See below for which license applies to which code.


1. Foundation Packages (MIT License)
-------------------------------------

The following packages in packages/ are licensed under the MIT License.
See licenses/MIT.txt for the full text.

  - @flow-arts/core         (packages/flow-arts-core/)
  - @tka/domain             (packages/domain/)
  - @vtg/domain             (packages/vtg-domain/)
  - @spin-science/domain    (packages/spin-science-domain/)
  - @caps/domain            (packages/caps-domain/)
  - @9square/domain         (packages/9square-domain/)
  - @tka/tka-types          (packages/tka-types/)
  - @austencloud/feedback-types (packages/feedback-types/)

These packages encode domain knowledge, shared types, and foundational
logic. They are freely available for anyone to use, modify, and
redistribute under the terms of the MIT License.


2. Rendering & Engine Packages (MIT License)
---------------------------------------------

The following packages are also MIT-licensed to enable community tooling:

  - @tka/render-core        (packages/render-core/)
  - @tka/sequence-engine    (packages/sequence-engine/)

These provide platform-agnostic calculation and rendering primitives.


3. TKA Composer Application (Elastic License 2.0)
---------------------------------------------------

Everything in src/ and the following packages are licensed under the
Elastic License 2.0. See licenses/ELv2.txt for the full text.

  - The full Composer application (src/)
  - @tka/render-composition (packages/render-composition/)
  - @tka/pictograph         (packages/pictograph/)
  - @tka/animation-renderer (packages/animation-renderer/)

This includes but is not limited to:
  - The 55+ feature modules (src/lib/features/)
  - Avatar animation system (3D rendering, hand poses, leg animation)
  - TIKA conversational AI tutor
  - Museum / gamification layer
  - Premium gating and subscription system
  - All UI components, layouts, and styling

You may use, copy, and modify this code freely EXCEPT:
  - You may NOT provide it as a hosted or managed service
  - You may NOT circumvent any license key or premium gating functionality
  - You may NOT remove or obscure copyright and license notices

See licenses/ELv2.txt for the legally binding terms.


4. MCP Servers (Elastic License 2.0)
--------------------------------------

  - flow-arts-knowledge-mcp (mcp-server/)
  - @tka/mcp-game-controller (packages/mcp-game-controller/)
  - @tka/mcp-tika-talk      (packages/mcp-tika-talk/)

The MCP domain knowledge server and related tooling are part of the
commercial platform.


5. Data & Datasets (Mixed Licensing)
--------------------------------------

5a. Open Sequence Data (CC BY-SA 4.0)

The following data is licensed under Creative Commons
Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International (CC BY-SA 4.0).
See licenses/CC-BY-SA-4.0.txt for the full text.

  - Sequence datasets (53,000+ enumerated sequences)
  - Deck composition data (deck lists, sequence groupings)
  - Pictograph reference data

You are free to share, print, teach from, and redistribute this data
provided you give attribution to Austen Cloud / The Kinetic Alphabet
and share any derivative datasets under the same license.

5b. Proprietary Data (All Rights Reserved)

The following data is proprietary and NOT licensed for redistribution:

  - Humor training pairs and AI fine-tuning data
  - ML training data and model weights
  - User-generated content (owned by the respective users)
  - Internal analytics and telemetry data

No license is granted for proprietary data. Contact
austencloud@gmail.com for commercial licensing inquiries.


6. Documentation & Notation Specification
------------------------------------------

Documentation describing the TKA notation system (the alphabet,
letter types, position theory, orientation rules) is licensed under
Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International (CC BY-SA 4.0).
See licenses/CC-BY-SA-4.0.txt for the full text.

This ensures the notation system itself remains an open standard that
anyone can teach, reference, and build upon, while requiring attribution
to Austen Cloud and TKA.


7. Post-Mortem Open Source Provision
--------------------------------------

It is the express intent of the sole copyright holder, Austen Cloud,
that upon his death or permanent incapacitation:

  (a) ALL code in this repository currently licensed under the Elastic
      License 2.0 (Sections 3 and 4 above) shall be automatically
      relicensed under the MIT License (licenses/MIT.txt).

  (b) ALL proprietary datasets (Section 5 above) shall be released
      under the Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0
      International License (licenses/CC-BY-SA-4.0.txt).

  (c) Components already under MIT or CC BY-SA 4.0 remain unchanged.

The purpose of this provision is to ensure that The Kinetic Alphabet
and all associated tools, knowledge, and data become freely available
to the global flow arts community and the public at large, in
perpetuity, should the original author no longer be able to steward
them.

Designated Executor: Fund the Flow Arts, Inc.
  501(c)(3) nonprofit, EIN 27-5073279
  https://fundtheflowarts.org

Fund the Flow Arts is designated as the organizational executor of
this provision. Their responsibilities upon the triggering event are:

  1. Verify the triggering event (death or permanent incapacitation
     of Austen Cloud)
  2. Change all LICENSE files in this repository and any related
     repositories under github.com/austencloud to reflect the
     relicensing described in (a), (b), and (c) above
  3. Publish a public announcement to the flow arts community
  4. Ensure continued public access to the repository

Fund the Flow Arts is NOT responsible for ongoing maintenance,
development, or hosting of the software. Their role is solely to
execute the relicensing. The community maintains the code thereafter.

This declaration of intent is supplemented by binding instructions in
the author's estate planning documents.

If you believe this provision has been triggered and the repository has
not yet been relicensed, contact Fund the Flow Arts directly or file
a public issue on the GitHub repository.


